# Competency question: "Which result kinds are frequentist?" Exercises the paradigm
# taxonomy: every frequentist inference result is asserted a DIRECT subclass of
# math:FrequentistResult in module.ttl, so the reasoning-free query walks the asserted
# rdfs:subClassOf edge (no closure needed) and enumerates the frequentist result vocabulary.
# Scoped to the math: namespace so a stray owl:Restriction blank never leaks in. Over the
# merged ontology the answer is exactly the six frequentist result kinds
# {math:PValue, math:StatisticalPower, math:TypeIErrorRate, math:TypeIIErrorRate,
# math:ConfidenceInterval, math:ConfidenceRegion}.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>

SELECT ?kind WHERE {
    ?kind rdfs:subClassOf math:FrequentistResult .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?kind), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?kind
